<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sala (Hoysala founder)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sala is the legendary founder of the Hoysala dynasty of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. According to the dynasty's tradition, a Jain teacher at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosevur">Sosevur</a> cried out to him to strike a tiger that threatened them, with the words hoy Sala, strike, Sala, and his victory gave the line its name. The scene of Sala killing the tiger became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> emblem, carved on many of their temples.</p></div>
